---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '@studpilot/shared';

// WHAT THIS PAGE IS FOR. StudPilot is in beta and free, and paid plans start later: checkout is OFF, so nobody can pay yet. The page says that first,
// and then says how billing will work once it opens (a failed card, invoices, cancelling, a plan that has not applied), so the rules are readable
// before anyone is subject to them. It was five long sections of paid-account procedure; it is the short version.
//
// EVERY CLAIM BELOW IS READ OFF apps/worker/src/billing.ts, not imagined, and tests/billing-help.test.mjs checks the two load-bearing ones against
// that file: that `past_due` still entitles (so "your plan keeps working while the card is retried" stays true), and that a lapsed period still drops
// to free. If someone tightens either rule, this page goes red naming the sentence that became a lie.
//
// THE ANSWER IS A FACT, NOT A PROBE (M2). It used to be asked of the live deployment at build time (/api/billing/config), which made a build depend
// on the network. Checkout is off and paid plans start later (planning/proof/M2/DECISIONS.md section 3), so the page says so; the day charging
// starts it is changed on purpose, with /pricing and its tests in the same change. tests/hermetic-build.test.mjs holds it.
const checkoutOpen = false;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Billing & payments | StudPilot"
  description={checkoutOpen
    ? 'What happens when a payment fails, where invoices live, how cancelling works, and what to do when a payment went through but the plan has not changed.'
    : 'Paid checkout is not open in the beta, so nobody can subscribe yet. How billing will work once it is: failed payments, invoices, cancelling and changing plan.'}
  heading="Billing & payments"
  order={4}
  summary="There is nothing to pay for in the beta. How billing will work when paid plans start."
>
  {!checkoutOpen && (
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>There is no way to become a paying customer yet.</strong> StudPilot is free while in beta and paid checkout is not open.
        <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> marks every paid plan "planned", and <a href="/terms">Terms</a> says the same. What follows describes how
        billing will work for a paid account. It applies to nobody today, and it is published so the rules can be read before anyone is subject to
        them. The Free plan is on <a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits &amp; limits</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  )}

  <p>
    Everything to do with money (cards, invoices, cancelling) lives in the billing portal, which is Stripe's, not ours. You reach it from
    <strong>Usage</strong> in the app (<a href="/app/usage">/app/usage</a>), from the button that reads <em>Manage billing, invoices and
    cancellation</em>. It appears once you are on a paid plan.
  </p>

  <h2 id="failed-payment">A payment failed or the card was declined</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Your plan keeps working.</strong> A failed renewal is usually an expired card, and a paying customer is not cut off at the first retry.
    Stripe retries over the following days, and for as long as it is retrying you keep the allowance you are paying for. Update the card in the
    billing portal and it applies at once. If Stripe gives up first, the subscription ends and the account drops to Free. Your projects, checkpoints
    and conversations are untouched.
  </p>

  <h2 id="invoices">Where invoices and receipts are</h2>
  <p>
    In the billing portal, under your payment history: every invoice, with a PDF. StudPilot keeps no second copy of your billing history. If you need
    a company name or a VAT number on an invoice, set it in the portal before the next one is issued.
  </p>

  <h2 id="cancelling">Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    Cancel in the billing portal. <strong>You keep the plan until the end of the period you have already paid for.</strong> After that date the
    account is on Free, with everything still in it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="not-applied">I paid, and the plan still shows the old one</h2>
  <p>
    Give it a few seconds and press <em>Check again</em> on the Usage page. Plans are applied from Stripe's own webhook rather than from the page you
    land on after paying, so a person who pays and closes the tab has still bought the plan. If it is still wrong after a minute, write in instead of
    paying again.
  </p>

  {/*
    Extra Credits are not for sale: no plan has a credit checkout, and /pricing says so in its comparison table. The behaviour that exists (a separate
    balance that outlives a subscription and is spent after the day's allowance) has no way to be reached today, so it is not described here.
  */}
  <h2 id="charges">What is charged, and what is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Nothing is charged before checkout completes.</strong> Starting one and closing it costs nothing.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Running out of Credits is not a charge.</strong> A request refused for lack of allowance is refused before it costs anything. See
      <a href="/docs/credits-and-limits">Credits &amp; limits</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A step that failed is not charged.</strong> Credits come from the compute a call actually reports, so a call that returned nothing
      reports nothing. <a href="/docs/troubleshooting#model-failures">Troubleshooting</a> covers what each failure means.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      A billing question a page cannot answer is worth an email: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>. Include the email address
      on the account and roughly when the payment was. Never send a card number: nobody at StudPilot needs it.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
